        <section name="DavMail Setup on windows">
            <p>DavMail installer now includes Azul JRE with OpenJFX support, so you no longer need to install Java
                separately.
            </p>

            <p>Easiest way to install and update DavMail on windows is using winget.
            </p>
            <source>winget install mguessan.davmail</source>
            <p>More information at: <a href="https://winstall.app/apps/mguessan.davmail">Install or upgrade DavMail with winget</a>.
            </p>

            <p>When we publish the winget package, Microsoft scans and validates the installer, which helps avoid
                issues with Windows Defender SmartScreen.
            </p>

            <p>When downloading the installer directly, if you are blocked by SmartScreen, you can explicitly unblock it
                with the following PowerShell command:
            </p>
            <source>Unblock-File .\davmail-*-setup64.exe</source>

            <p>DavMail setup is straightforward, just follow the setup wizard.
